                    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">It gives great pleasure to recognize the recipient of this year's AOS Distinguished Alumni Award, Dr. {{ recipient_full_name }} ({{ recipient_graduation_year }}), and Ph.D. ({{ recipient_phd_year }}), in the then-Meteorology Department at the University of Wisconsin-Madison. He made fundamental</p>
                    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">contributions to ground, aircraft, and satellite based infrared radiation measurements for infrared sounding of the Earth's atmosphere. The award is presented by the AOS Alumni Reception to be held in conjunction with the American Meteorological Society Annual Meeting in Houston, TX, on Tuesday, January 25, 2021. A fuller biography can be found on our website: <a href="{{ bio_link }}">https://www.aos.wisc.edu/</a></p>
